# finish-recursive-dynamodb-capabilities-1545: completion report

`@endo/exo-dynamodb` now matches the final design (kriscendobot/minion.town#221 at d65ac219e6). I pushed one commit, e728a830fa, onto `gardener/fu-design-recursive-dynamodb-capabilities-1` and updated draft PR https://github.com/endojs/endo-but-for-bots/pull/1545, keeping its garden job marker. In this PR's CI the package's own tests pass (39 passed, 2 skipped). All the failing checks are failures already present on other branches. Two integration tests could not run against the real target (details below).

## What changed
- **derive, withdraw, lineage:** both `derive` methods now return a result carrying the capability and its grant id. The host control has async `withdraw` and `lineage`, plus a `retire()` call used at restart. Malformed, widening, conflicting or revoked requests come back as results instead of rejected promises, and every `limit-exceeded` result says which limit was hit.
- **Restriction shape:** restrictions now use `keySpace`, per-index key-range maps, a nested `shape` (with a `guard` condition), `operations`, and limits `pageSize`, `transactionSize`, `itemBytes` and `requestsPerSecond`. Omitted parts inherit from the parent; a child that names anything outside its parent is refused rather than silently clamped.
- **Guards:** a guard may only combine equality, begins-with and existence tests with AND (plus negating a single test). Updates check guard fields they touch directly, enforce untouched ones as a DynamoDB condition, and refuse add/delete on a guarded field.
- **Keys and queries:** numeric sort keys accept exact values or closed intervals, and a query's sort condition is intersected with the one allowed range it selects.
- **Index queries:** rows outside any ancestor's base key space or guard are dropped with no count of dropped rows. Consistent reads on global secondary indexes are refused.
- **Idempotency:** individual writes and transactions accept idempotency keys. Tokens are tied to the grant and capped at 36 characters; the old implementation sent 64, which DynamoDB rejects.
- **Durable named grants:** recipes and withdrawal tombstones go through an injected grant store. `reincarnateDynamoControl` reads tombstones first and rebinds only live named grants.
- **Binary values:** they now cross the boundary as passable frozen byte arrays. Plain `Uint8Array` was rejected by the exo guard, so binary data was unusable before.
- **Other changes:**
  - New optional host `log` power for full provider diagnostics.
  - New `@endo/immutable-arraybuffer` dependency, with `yarn.lock` and the composite tsconfig updated.
  - README and changeset rewritten.

**Tests:** the suite covers property-generated three-level chains, deny-before-send, index leakage, guards, sort narrowing, positional transaction cancellation, paging, idempotency, error redaction, revocation (including just before dispatch and in flight), restart with tombstones, audit, and a confined-compartment escape attempt. It runs against a new in-memory fake DynamoDB that parses the compiled expressions.

**Checks run:** package tests (40 pass with the integration test enabled), package ESLint (no errors), package and repo-root `tsc`, `prettier --check`, the composite-tsconfig drift check, and the composite build.

